 "limits": [
  "the row table is E625's; this study does not re-parse the modules, so a read E625 missed is invisible here -- the coverage count is the guard, not a re-derivation",
  "reads are counted at name level as E625 spelled them; a read through an alias of the receiver inside the interval is E627's arm, not this one",
  "the dead line itself is excluded from the after-list by construction (strictly greater line number), so two reads on one physical line read as one site",
  "multiplicity is priced only as a denominator question: this study does not re-ask the value test for the second and third read",
  "the population is E625's 34 live lines; the 2 inert lines and 14 skipped modules stay outside it exactly as E625 published them"
 ],
 "verdict": "3_of_34_lines_carry_more_than_one_read_after_the_dead_line_but_e625_enumerated_every_read_so_the_duplicate_denominator_stands",
 "answer": "E625 published 34 live dead face-key lines with 13 read(s) of the key after the dead line in total, spread over 6 line(s); 3 line(s) carry more than one such read and 3 of the 4 duplicate rows sit in a function that holds more than two reads. Because E625's sibling_reads list accounts for every read in the function on all 34 covered line(s) (0 uncovered), the duplicate test already saw the second and third read, so the multiplicity changes no published count -- the concern E631 was opened to price is empty in this population, and it is empty by measurement, not by assumption."
}
